**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`

**How to implement.** The linear engine is the staged Mueller path driven by a study (001 §L 'the linear path is `MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign` + `reconstruct`'; the S11.3 brief 'S10.3's staged path'), so the pieces of that path the study needs become callable, each MOVED out of a private helper and called back by the reference path, not copied (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). Every number of the reference path is computed by the same operations in the same order, so `MuellerReconstructionTests` is bit-identical. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: `Family` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:Family`) gains `member this.text : string` (`LP-LP`, `LP-CPL`, `CPL-LP`, `CPL-CPL`) and `MatrixKind` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixKind`) `member this.text : string` (`AIR`, `QZ`, `LR`, `QZ+LR`); `SolverError` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:SolverError`) gains `member this.describe : string` (`the design is singular: <reason>`, `the design is rank-deficient: rank <n>`); `AnalyzerModel` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:AnalyzerModel`) gains `static member linearAt (zero : Angle) (sign : DialSign) : AnalyzerModel` (`IdealLinear`, no retarder) and `static member circularAt (zero : Angle) (sign : DialSign) (retardance : Retardance) : AnalyzerModel` (`IdealCircularLeft`, `thetaRelOpt = Some (Angle.degree 45.0<deg>)`, `retardanceOpt = Some (Retardance.degree (- retardance.degrees * 1.0<deg>))`, the stage-one expression of step 349, so the same double); and `LeastSquaresSystem` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:LeastSquaresSystem`) gains `static member ofProjections (projections : (StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity) list) : LeastSquaresSystem` (each `designRow s a` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:designRow`) and its signal, in order), the assembly `buildDesign` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:buildDesign`) ends with today, which it now calls, and `static member concat (systems : LeastSquaresSystem list) : LeastSquaresSystem` (design rows and right-hand sides in list order), the concatenation `reconstructStaged` makes (step 351), which it now calls. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs` (steps 349-356): (a) `StageOneAirRows = { darknessRows : MuellerRawRow list; lpLpAirRows : MuellerRawRow list; lpCplAirRows : MuellerRawRow list; cplLpAirRows : MuellerRawRow list }` and `calibrateFromAirRows (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (rows : StageOneAirRows) : Result<StageOneCalibrationData, StagedMuellerError>`, the body of `calibrateStageOne` moved over AIR rows the caller selected: the private `reduceAirTraces` loses its AIR-label filter, and `calibrateStageOne solver captures` becomes `calibrateFromAirRows` of the darkness rows and of each family file's rows whose label holds `(AIR#0)`, the filter it applied, so the same rows reach the same traces. (b) `airAnchorGainOf (source : SourceModel) (analyzer : AnalyzerModel) (dark : DarkMean) (run : ExperimentName) (rows : MuellerRawRow list) : Result<AirAnchorGain, StagedMuellerError>` (`AirAnchorGain`, step 356), the private `fitAirGain` and `meanTime` of step 351 moved: `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming the run for no row; else `scalarGain` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:scalarGain`) of the rows' `darkSubtract` signals against `airIdentityPred` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:airIdentityPred`) of `source.baseStokes` and `analyzerBaseRow analyzer r.description`, at the rows' mean capture time; `reconstructStaged` calls it for its nine anchors. (c) `projectCaptureRow (source : SourceModel) (analyzer : AnalyzerModel) (phi : Angle) (dark : DarkMean) (gain : AirGain) (row : MuellerRawRow) : StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity`, the private `prepareRow` of step 351 moved: `effectiveSource phi source.baseStokes`, `effectiveAnalyzer phi (analyzerBaseRow analyzer row.description)` and `correctSignal dark row.avgTotal gain` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:effectiveSource`, `:effectiveAnalyzer`, `:correctSignal`); `reconstructStaged`'s projections call it with the reading's `objectPhi` and the session rule's `gainAt row.capturedAt`. (d) `StageOneCalibrationData.lpAnalyzer` and `cplAnalyzer` (step 349) are `AnalyzerModel.linearAt this.lpZero DialNegative` and `AnalyzerModel.circularAt this.cplZero DialPositive this.cplAnalyzerRetardance`. (e) `StagedMuellerError` gains `member this.describe : string`, each case's condition and payload: `a set of capture rows the staged path needs is empty: <reason>`, `the AIR cosine fit of <family text> failed: <the solver error's describe>`, `the reconstruction of <kind text> failed: <the solver error's describe>` and `a session gain model was refused: <the study error's describe>`. No other declaration of either file changes, and no BerremanTests file is edited. Tests, in `StagedMuellerPathTests` (step 349), over its synthetic captures (step 351): `stage one over AIR rows given directly equals stage one over the files that hold them`: `calibrateStageOne` over the files equals, field by field and exactly, `calibrateFromAirRows` over their darkness rows and their `(AIR#0)` rows; `an AIR anchor's gain scales its ideal prediction onto its dark-subtracted signal, at its rows' mean time`: two LP-LP AIR rows at dials 0° and 40°, captured at 10:00 and 10:02, whose `avgTotal` is 3 · `airIdentityPred` of `LpSource.baseStokes` and `analyzerBaseRow (AnalyzerModel.linearAt Angle.zero DialPositive)` at the dial, plus 5, give `airAnchorGainOf` a gain of 3 within 1e-12 at 10:01 for `DarkMean 5`, and no row `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming the run; `a capture row is projected into its object frame and its signal corrected by the dark and the gain`: `projectCaptureRow` of a CPL source, a circular analyzer, φ 30°, dark 5 and gain 2 equals the three expressions above exactly, and `LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections` of two projections holds their two `designRow`s and signals, `concat` of two systems their rows in order; `the stage-one analyzer and source models are the shared calibrated models of its constants`: a stage-one constant set's `lpAnalyzer` and `cplAnalyzer` equal `linearAt` and `circularAt` of its zeros and retardance, field by field; `every staged path error renders its condition and its payload`: each `StagedMuellerError` case over a distinct test-local payload renders a distinct text holding its payload's text (`LP-CPL` for `AirCalibrationFitErr (LpCpl, SingularDesignErr "x")`), each `Family` and `MatrixKind` its text and each `SolverError` its describe. `MuellerReconstructionTests` runs unchanged, every number bit-identical.

**Acceptance.** After the moves, `calibrateFromAirRows`, `airAnchorGainOf`, `projectCaptureRow`, `LeastSquaresSystem.ofProjections` / `concat` and `AnalyzerModel.linearAt` / `circularAt` MUST be public with the reference path calling them and keeping no private copy, and every staged path error MUST render through `describe`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `stage one over AIR rows given directly equals stage one over the files that hold them`, `an AIR anchor's gain scales its ideal prediction onto its dark-subtracted signal, at its rows' mean time`, `a capture row is projected into its object frame and its signal corrected by the dark and the gain`, `the stage-one analyzer and source models are the shared calibrated models of its constants` and `every staged path error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; unit-tests MUST pass over `MuellerReconstructionTests` with every number unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.
